Z||000000||EdsB52||07-03-2001||06:24 PM||||Posted by 1FST2M6;<P><BR>"must really take alot to threaten somone over the internet... it is his board and he can do what he wants. he never askes for $ and usually keeps the riff raff out."<P>I agree. Cliff wrote;<P>"Ed, you have just gone too far. I'll be in the States in two weeks. Expect to be contacted then."<P>I haven't threatened Cliff or anyone in here. Now did Cliff mean that he would have someone 'contact' me, or that he would do it himself? Did he imply physical violence, property damage, or something litigious? He didn't specify, so can I assume the worse? Besides, how could he have meant litigious contact when he isn't running a commercial venture here? In order to sue, there must be damages. If he could argue punitive damages for mental distress relating to me participating in his forum for which I'm not banned, then he's (or his lawyers are) good. I think I've successfully argued that Cliff did not mean litigious contact with his threatening statement. I think two things are true; first, he meant physical or property damage. Second, he will not do anything, and if he does, the most he's capable of is property damage. Generally speaking, people who are going to act don't spout off. Cliff sure has a lot of cheerleaders behind him though. Seems that practically the entire forum is backing him. I wonder what percent of them actually have a good understanding of how this started? Good thing I'm not the kind of person that hinges my self-perception around what others think of me.||||reg||1
