Z||000017||Her86GT||07-03-2001||08:00 PM||||I'm glad something is finally being done about annoying people on this Forum.  It's too bad that some had to wreck it for the rest of us.  My husband enjoyed coming home from work, turning on the computer and sitting on the Forum all night helping others with their cars.  He's a GM technican and he brought home Fiero shop manuals to help people trouble shoot their vehicles.  <P>How this Fourm turned into a conspiracy is news to me.  I agree with Cliff in the fact that those who choose to get upset at people they don't know or whom they have NEVER met, should indeed get their head examined!!!||||reg||1
Z||000018||Raydar||07-03-2001||08:06 PM||||Ed. The fact of the matter is that Archie and Cliff are indeed two different individuals. I HAVE seen pictures of them both. No resemblance whatsoever. I was on this forum for quite a while before Archie joined, and had even communicated with him via a few e-mails. Just not the same person.<BR>As for Cliff's "hidden agenda"?<BR>The last I heard was that his digital instruments were not even available. Didn't know that had changed. He certainly hasn't felt the need to advertise them too awfully much. If you had been here for a while before you started the paranoid rant, you would have realized that.<BR>Anyway, It now appears that the Forum is shut down, so all I can say is "Thanks a Pantload".<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000019||EdsB52||07-03-2001||08:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>Cliff *has* closed the forum and I'm still his [b]#1</B> cheerleader.  If you get a chance to read this reply, please do me a favor and abstain from posting here again until you change your attitude.  I hope you've read Cliffs' new opening page.  He hasn't made any money here, he's busted his ass for a long time and gained nothing from it (financially), and he's tired of the BS.  I can't blame him. <P>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Monkeyman, you've always been very reasonable and rational in here, and still seem to be. Tell me why you think (know) the forum is gone. If this forum is gone, is it reasonable to blame it on this incident? I mean if someone is involved in something that they plan on staying with for some time, one incident won't dissuade them. If he pulls this it's because he was going to anyway. Look at how this issue originated. Archie posted an advertisement for his stuff; I proposed a problem exists with any engine that produces massive torque and the marriage to the 2 available transmissions. He sharply disagreed and attacked me, club members blindly jumped in. I assembled a list of these folks, entered them, and the list was swiftly removed. Let's talk about the substantive issues here and get along, or not. I really want this forum to stay, as I write posts on it everyday, but if it goes my life goes on. The hate mail is rolling in as people are slamming the crap out of me. Does anyone think they're getting to me?||||reg||1
