Z||000095||stimpy||07-06-2001||09:52 AM||||Okie doke folks, I can see the bonfires burning. It's no secret that the general consensus is that Mr. Ed crossed a line. Just for clarity, that line was NOT in disagreeing with Archie. As Jeff (Black88GT) stated, that has happened to most of us who have been on the forum longer then 6 months. No big deal. The line was crossed when he posted a list of people who in Ed's esteem, were providing Archie with oral gratification. It was tacky, spurious, and generally uncalled for. FINE. Let it be.<P>Once upon a time, I got in a little sparring altercation with a member who had been on longer then I. By it being public, it progressed to getting nastier and nastier. It didn't matter who was right or wrong, just who had seen their name on the forum more. Eventually I lost my cool and crossed the line. Fortunately, there wasn't this witch hunt tempermant then, and I was able to back out gracefully. I hope that people can get the taste of blood out of their mouths and just let it be.<P>Now, does that make me an admirer of Eds? No, I think he is an egomaniacal control freak who has some issues with his latent sexuality (hence the repetitive references to others imagined deviant behavior), but everyones got their weak points. I'm sure if you folks castinmg stones stick around for another thousand or so posts, you'll piss someone off too. So take a break from throwing stones and polish your glass houses for a change.<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
