Z||000097||EdsB52||07-06-2001||10:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>Okie doke folks, I can see the bonfires burning. It's no secret that the general consensus is that Mr. Ed crossed a line. Just for clarity, that line was NOT in disagreeing with Archie. As Jeff (Black88GT) stated, that has happened to most of us who have been on the forum longer then 6 months. No big deal. The line was crossed when he posted a list of people who in Ed's esteem, were providing Archie with oral gratification. It was tacky, spurious, and generally uncalled for. FINE. Let it be.<P>Once upon a time, I got in a little sparring altercation with a member who had been on longer then I. By it being public, it progressed to getting nastier and nastier. It didn't matter who was right or wrong, just who had seen their name on the forum more. Eventually I lost my cool and crossed the line. Fortunately, there wasn't this witch hunt tempermant then, and I was able to back out gracefully. I hope that people can get the taste of blood out of their mouths and just let it be.<P>Now, does that make me an admirer of Eds? No, I think he is an egomaniacal control freak who has some issues with his latent sexuality (hence the repetitive references to others imagined deviant behavior), but everyones got their weak points. I'm sure if you folks castinmg stones stick around for another thousand or so posts, you'll piss someone off too. So take a break from throwing stones and polish your glass houses for a change.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>See, just when grinthock (who has taken his fair share of shots) steps in to try to put this to rest, some rank oriented jerk-off jumps in. And you think you would make a good moderator? The idea for moderation is to create continuity within the Fiero community by keeping the forum on track. Don't keep referring to my actions, although I feel I have been fully justified to defame who I have (don't we all think we're right). Look at the only actions you have control of, yours. And what do you do, jump in when a situation is winding down and stir the pot. Good job moderator wanna-be.<P>Who crossed the line with who doesn't matter, it's a matter of opinion. Consensus only means a generally majority of people feel that way. How many people out of 2,737 have spoken out against me? Less than 100? Consensus? I am still receiving a few emails of agreement.<P>"I got in a little sparring altercation with a member who had been on longer then I."<P>Who cares? That statement shows how you buy into this rank-privilege crap. It works in the military, but it's a joke in here. All your doing is reinforcing my contention that guys like Archie carry more weight in here due to his status, regardless of how right / wrong he might be.<P>"No, I think he is an egomaniacal control freak who has some issues with his latent sexuality (hence the repetitive references to others imagined deviant behavior), but everyone’s got their weak points."<P>And who wants to be the moderator? What a self-defining statement by someone who wants to be in a position of control. My vote is that you're not a moderator. Not because you disagree with me, think everything is all my fault, or buy into your fractional consensus theory, but because you are stirring the pot for which there is no need.||||reg||1
